  "summary_en": "Peer-reviewed paper proposing that Care Centered Value Sensitive Design, developed for healthcare robots, can be extended to personal and professional service robots when they are integrated into a care practice. It sets two conditions for a care practice and illustrates them with robot prototypes.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Service robots (about 35 million by 2018 per IFR) demand ethical attention because they appear to be moral agents and are placed in ethically charged contexts.",
   "CCVSD can be applied outside healthcare when a robot is integrated into a care practice.",
   "A care practice must respond to the needs of another.",
   "A care practice must meet those needs through reciprocal interaction between care giver and care receiver.",
   "Robots outside care practices should not be evaluated with CCVSD; the paper is a preliminary study."
